Dependency license inventory
============================
Reviewed: 2026-09-17
Reference layout: https://github.com/datakaveri/dx-controlplane/blob/main/dep-licenses

Scope
-----
Direct dependencies declared in package.json and the three requirements.txt files.
Node.js versions are resolved versions from pnpm-lock.yaml. Python exact pins use
version-specific PyPI metadata; ranges are checked at their declared lower bound
and do not establish the license of every permitted version.
License labels come from official npm/PyPI metadata. Long license fields are
summarized; linked metadata includes full notices and bundled-component licenses.
This is not a full transitive-dependency, container-image, service, or legal
compatibility audit. Third-party licenses and notices remain applicable; the root
AGPL license does not replace them. Recheck when dependencies change.

Review items
------------
metrics==0.0.2 and dotenv==0.9.9 do not declare a license in their PyPI
license fields/classifiers. Verify their distributed license files and
redistribution permission with upstream before treating them as approved.
chardet reports only "LGPL"; verify its exact version and notices in the artifact.
pandas and numpy include bundled-component notices: inspect the linked metadata
and actual distribution artifacts rather than relying only on the primary label.
External server software and image contents require a separate version-specific
review; this inventory must not be taken as public-release clearance.

